.git
.github/
.t3/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/__pycache__/
# Installed and built inside the stages that need them — a host copy would both
# bloat the context and shadow the image's own install (server/node_modules would
# land on top of the runtime's production-only tree).
**/node_modules/
server/dist/
web/dist/
# The HARNESSES stay out of the image — but their MANIFESTS have to come in. yarn resolves
# the lockfile against every workspace named in the root `workspaces`, so an absent
# e2e/package.json makes `yarn install --immutable` fail before it installs anything. Docker
# (unlike git) honours a re-include for a file inside an excluded directory, and last match
# wins — so these two lines must stay AFTER `e2e/`.
e2e/
!e2e/package.json
!e2e/broker/package.json
__screenshots__/
.env
.env.local
docs/
*.md
